config ATM_BROWNOUT
	bool "Enable brownout support"
	default y if PM

if ATM_BROWNOUT

config BROWNOUT_THR_VBAT
        int "VBAT brownout threshold"
        default 0
        help
            Controls the VBAT(LI) brownout threshold.
            For VBAT level <= 1.8V,
                VBAT threshold = 0.9 + 0.025X, where 0 <= X <= 31
            For VBAT level > 1.8V,
                VBAT threshold = 1.4 + 0.05X, where
                    0 <= X <= 31, for non-rechargeable battery type
                    0 <= X <= 17, for rechargeable battery type
	    For VBATLI,
		VBATLI threshold = 2.4V + 0.050X, where 2 <= X <= 31
            The battery level is specified through OTP and is equal to BATT_LEVEL_GT_1P8V by default. It can be overwritten through the ``batt-level`` device tree property. Refer to the PMU configuration for additional details.

config BROWNOUT_THR_VSTORE
        int "VSTORE brownout threshold"
        range -1 31
        default -1
        help
            Controls the VSTORE brownout threshold for non-lithium ion battery types.
            VSTORE threshold = 0.7 + 0.05X, where 0 <= X <= 31

            Set to -1 (default) to use automatic battery-type-dependent defaults:
            - Rechargeable batteries: 31 (fixed, cannot be overridden)
            - Non-rechargeable batteries: 0

            Set to 0-31 to explicitly specify the threshold value.

            Note: For rechargeable batteries, this value is enforced to be 31
            in the driver code regardless of the configured value.

            The chip enters brownout if both VBAT and VSTORE are below their
            configured thresholds.

config BROWNOUT_THR_VBAT_HYSTERESIS_DELTA
        int "VBAT brownout hysteresis delta"
        range 0 31
        default 10
        help
            Delta value added to BROWNOUT_THR_VBAT when increasing the VBAT
            brownout threshold for hysteresis during hibernation entry.

            When entering hibernation due to brownout, the VBAT threshold is
            temporarily increased by this delta to provide hysteresis and
            prevent rapid on/off cycling near the brownout threshold.

            The effective threshold is clamped to a maximum of 31.

            Set to 0 to disable hysteresis (not recommended).

endif
